<!-- Origin story — visual timeline (2.5) preserves human specifics -->
<section id="story" class="card" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="story-heading">How GatherPack Got Started</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <ol class="list-unstyled position-relative ps-4 mb-0" style="border-left: 3px solid #a59e86;">
      <li class="mb-4 ps-3">
        <h3 class="h5 mb-1"><time datetime="2014">2014</time> — The problem</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">A <a href="https://boilerinvasion.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FIRST Robotics team</a> couldn't keep its information straight. Attendance records, fundraising progress, and competition logistics were scattered across spreadsheets, sticky notes, and the heads of whoever happened to be available to ask.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-4 ps-3">
        <h3 class="h5 mb-1"><time datetime="2014">2014–2015</time> — The first fix</h3>
        <p class="mb-0"><a href="https://brad-thompson.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">One volunteer web developer</a> built a small internal tool to pull it together — just enough to get the team through the season.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-4 ps-3">
        <h3 class="h5 mb-1"><time datetime="2015">2015–2024</time> — Growing with the team</h3>
        <p class="mb-0">That tool grew over the next decade into the operational backbone of <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">an organization</a> that has since quadrupled in size. What started as a quick fix became daily infrastructure.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-0 ps-3">
        <h3 class="h5 mb-1"><time datetime="2024">2024 — GatherPack today</time></h3>
        <p class="mb-0">When the original tool started showing its age, the same developer and a few students rebuilt it from scratch, this time with other organizations in mind — flexible enough for a 10-person club or a 500-person nonprofit. <a href="/about/">Read the full story →</a></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Open-source / self-host pillar (2.3) -->
<section id="open-source" class="card" aria-labelledby="open-source-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="open-source-heading">Open Source — Your Choice, Your Control</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>GatherPack is free, open-source software under the <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a>. Unlike SaaS-only tools, you decide how to run it.</p>
    <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-card h-100">
          <div class="feature-card__icon">
            <i class="fa-4x fa-brands fa-github" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card__body">
            <h3>Self-Host Free</h3>
            <p>Run GatherPack on your own server at no cost. Full access to the source, your data stays with you, customize anything.</p>
            <p class="mb-0"><a href="/open-source/">Learn about self-hosting →</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
        <div class="feature-card h-100">
          <div class="feature-card__icon">
            <i class="fa-4x fa-solid fa-cloud" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </div>
          <div class="feature-card__body">
            <h3>Managed Hosting via Sledgehammer</h3>
            <p>Prefer not to run servers? <a href="https://sledgehammerinfosystems.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sledgehammer Infosystems</a> handles hosting, updates, and support.</p>
            <p class="mb-0"><a href="/hosting/">Compare hosting options →</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="table-responsive mt-4">
      <table class="table table-bordered align-middle mb-0">
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Comparison of self-hosted vs managed hosting</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Self-Host Free</th>
            <th scope="col">Managed Hosting</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">License &amp; cost</th>
            <td>MIT — $0</td>
            <td>Standard $50/mo · Custom $100/mo + plugins</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">You manage</th>
            <td>Server, updates, backups, payment integrations</td>
            <td>Nothing — we handle it, including Stripe</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Best for</th>
            <td>Teams with technical chops who want full control</td>
            <td>Teams who want it to just work</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-0 small text-muted">Both options are the same GatherPack. <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Roadmap reframed (2.4) — Available now vs On the roadmap, no asterisk footnote -->
<section id="roadmap" class="card" aria-labelledby="roadmap-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="roadmap-heading">What's Ready &amp; What's Next</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p class="mb-4">GatherPack is in active development. Here's what's running today and what's intentionally next — not hidden gaps, but a visible plan.</p>
    <div class="row g-4">
      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
        <h3 class="h5">Available now</h3>
        <ul class="mb-0">
          <li>Member management — roster, teams, managers, badges</li>
          <li>Event management — RSVP, custom fields, shifts &amp; check-in</li>
          <li>Time tracking — kiosk, PIN/barcode/RFID, period reporting</li>
          <li>Finance — ledger, tagged transactions, receipts, Stripe payments</li>
          <li>Communication — team-scoped announcements, email summaries</li>
          <li>Automation — custom reports</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 col-md-6">
        <h3 class="h5">On the roadmap</h3>
        <ul class="mb-0">
          <li>Multi-channel messaging — text, Slack, Discord</li>
          <li>Notifications for RSVPs, payments, new members</li>
          <li>Actions — user-triggered custom tasks</li>
          <li>Hooks — automatic logic on system events</li>
          <li>Calendar sync — Google Calendar and more</li>
          <li>Finance — Zeffy, PayPal, Venmo; bank-pull transactions</li>
          <li>Organization — titles &amp; org charts</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-0"><a href="/roadmap/">See the full roadmap with dates →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

